RESUME SKILL GAP ANALYZER - AUTHENTICATION SYSTEM
================================================================

1. OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Complete authentication system with:
- Password hashing (bcrypt)
- JWT tokens (60 day expiry)
- Refresh token support
- Protected routes


2. TECHNOLOGIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- bcrypt: Password hashing (industry standard)
- python-jose: JWT token generation/decode
- FastAPI: HTTPBearer for protected routes


3. SECURITY FEATURES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3.1 Password Hashing
- Algorithm: bcrypt with automatic salt
- Cost factor: Default (12 rounds)
- Stored: Full hash (not encrypted password)

3.2 JWT Tokens
- Algorithm: HS256
- Secret: From settings.SECRET_KEY
- Expiry: 60 days
- Claims: sub (user_id), email, exp

3.3 Refresh Tokens
- Separate from access token
- Same expiry (60 days)
- Can be used to generate new access token


4. API ENDPOINTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

POST /api/v1/auth/register
Request:
{
    "name": "John Doe",
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
}
Response:
{
    "access_token": "eyJhbGc...",
    "refresh_token": "eyJhbGc...",
    "token_type": "bearer",
    "expires_in": 60
}

POST /api/v1/auth/login
Request:
{
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
}
Response:
{
    "access_token": "eyJhbGc...",
    "refresh_token": "eyJhbGc...",
    "token_type": "bearer",
    "expires_in": 60
}

POST /api/v1/auth/refresh
Request:
{
    "refresh_token": "eyJhbGc..."
}
Response:
{
    "access_token": "new_token...",
    "refresh_token": "new_refresh...",
    "token_type": "bearer",
    "expires_in": 60
}

GET /api/v1/auth/me (Protected)
Headers: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
Response:
{
    "id": "abc123...",
    "name": "John Doe",
    "email": "john@example.com"
}

POST /api/v1/auth/logout
Response:
{"message": "Logged out successfully"}


5. CODE STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 app/security.py
- hash_password(password): Hash password using bcrypt
- verify_password(plain, hashed): Verify password
- create_access_token(data, expiry): Create JWT access token
- decode_access_token(token): Decode and verify JWT
- create_refresh_token(data): Create refresh token


4.2 app/routes/auth.py
- Dependencies:
  - get_current_user(): Verify JWT and return user
- Protected routes use: Depends=get_current_user


6. USAGE IN FRONTEND
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Store tokens:
localStorage.setItem('access_token', response.access_token);
localStorage.setItem('refresh_token', response.refresh_token);

Include in requests:
fetch('/api/v1/analysis/analyze', {
    headers: {
        'Authorization': `Bearer ${access_token}`,
        'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    }
});


7. PRODUCTION RECOMMENDATIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Use database (PostgreSQL/MySQL) instead of in-memory store
- Add token blacklist for logout
- Implement rate limiting
- Add email verification
- Use HTTPS only
- Store SECRET_KEY in environment variables
- Add refresh token rotation
- Add 2FA support


